// Affinity overlay: the human-editable surface for evolving how cards DRAFT in
// the `embedded` pool variant. Each recipe is folded into the record-derived
// synergy matrix at bake time, before the card embedding is fit, so an added or
// re-pointed card lands in the synergy geometry next to the cards it resembles
// and receives a consistent latent vector automatically.
//
// Workflow:
//   1. Edit this file (see the shapes below). Cards are keyed by lowercase
//      cards_v2 UUID.
//   2. Run `npm run bake-affinity-corpus` to re-bake `data/affinity_embedding.json`.
//   3. Commit both this file and the regenerated embedding.
//
// To make an added/changed card count in the build-around QUALITY METRIC too,
// also add its theme entry to `data/buildaround_support.json` — that metadata
// system is independent of this overlay.
//
//   "add":  introduce a card absent from the historical records.
//     { "id": "<new-card-uuid>", "resembles": ["<uuidA>", "<uuidB>"], "priorScale": 1.0 }
//   "edit": re-point or rescale an existing card.
//     { "id": "<uuid>", "resembles": ["<uuidX>"], "priorScale": 0.8 }   // re-point + rescale
//     { "id": "<uuid>", "priorScale": 0.5 }                              // rescale only
//
//   `resembles` UUIDs may reference any base card or an earlier overlay `add`
//   (recipes are processed `add` then `edit`, each in array order).
//   `priorScale` defaults to 1.0.
{
  "add": [],
  "edit": []
}
